ation","subcommittees":[]},{"activities":[{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsju00","name":"Judiciary Committee","subcommittees":[]},{"activities":[{"date":"2026-05-14","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsgo00","name":"Oversight and Government Reform Committee","subcommittees":[]}],"cosponsor_count":110,"fetched_at":"2026-10-26T21:51:47+00:00","history":[{"day":"2026-10-26","importance":null,"viability":31.8},{"day":"2026-11-04","importance":85,"viability":31.8}],"id":"119-hr-8831","importance":85,"importance_band":"sweeping","importance_detail":{"consistent":true,"dimension_mean":85.0,"dimensions":[{"assessment":"Affects the President, Vice President, cabinet members, all federal agencies, executive branch officials, federal whistleblowers, political committees, candidates, and online platforms.","evidence":"To protect our democracy by preventing abuses of Presidential power, restoring checks and balances and accountability and transparency in government","evidence_verified":true,"key":"population","score":90},{"assessment":"Changes are major and life-changing for targeted executive branch and political figures, establishing criminal penalties, severe ethics and emoluments restrictions, and stripping certain presidential immunities.","evidence":"Any person who knowingly and willfully commits a violation of subsection (i) or (b)(9) of section 304 or section 302(j) shall be fined not more than $500,000, imprisoned not more than 5 years","evidence_verified":true,"key":"magnitude","score":85},{"assessment":"Substantial fiscal and economic implications through new reporting, civil and criminal monetary penalties, forfeiture of former presidential benefits, and online ad disclosures.","evidence":"a civil monetary penalty in an amount not to exceed $5,000 more than the retail value of the foreign payment","evidence_verified":true,"key":"fiscal","score":65},{"assessment":"A sweeping legislative overhaul that creates new statutory offices, amends criminal codes, alters federal agency and civil service rules, enforces congressional subpoenas, and modifies campaign finance and ethics laws.","evidence":"This Act is organized into divisions as follows: (1) Division A--Preventing Abuses of Presidential Power. (2) Division B--Restoring Checks and Balances, Accountability, and Transparency. (3) Division C--Miscellaneous. (4) Division D--Severability.","evidence_verified":true,"key":"scope","score":95},{"assessment":"Permanent changes to federal law, government accountability procedures, and election regulations, affecting all future administrations and Congresses.","evidence":null,"evidence_verified":false,"key":"duration","score":90}],"missing_information":["Exact figures on the total administrative cost to implement the new agency offices and reporting mechanisms are not specified."],"rationale":"The Protecting Our Democracy Act implements sweeping reforms across the federal government, presidential powers, congressional oversight, and election administration. It places major restrictions and transparency requirements on the President, Vice President, cabinet members, senior federal officials, federal employees, and political committees.","score":85},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-11-04T22:44:49+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr8831/BILLS-119hr8831ih.htm"]},"introduced_date":"2026-05-14","is_demo":false,"label":"H.R. 8831","latest_action":{"date":"2026-05-14","text":"Referred to the Committee on Oversight and Government Reform, and in addition to the Committees on the Judiciary, House Administration, the Budget, Transportation and Infrastructure, Rules, Foreign Affairs, Ways and Means, and Intelligence (Permanent Select), for a period to be subsequently determined by the Speaker, in each case for consideration of such provisions as fall within the jurisdiction of the committee concerned."},"members":[