31/BILLS-119hr8831ih.htm"},"other":[{"label":"This bill on Congress.gov","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/8831"}],"past":[]},"sponsor":{"chamber":"House","district":"8","id":"R000606","name":"Rep. Raskin, Jamie","party":"D","state":"MD"},"stage":"in_committee","stage_label":"Referred to committee","summary":"H.R. 8831, titled the \"Protecting Our Democracy Act,\" proposes a wide array of government reforms. The bill aims to prevent abuses of executive and presidential power, strengthen congressional checks and balances, increase transparency across federal agencies, establish stricter ethics and emoluments enforcement, protect whistleblowers, and defend elections against foreign interference.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"Face restrictions on self-pardons, acceptance of foreign and domestic emoluments, receipt of federal or state funds outside of official compensation, and tax return disclosure mandates.","group":"Presidents and Vice Presidents"},{"effect":"Receive enhanced protections against retaliatory personnel actions, protections for reporting research censorship, and expanded legal recourse through district court jury trials.","group":"Federal Employees and Whistleblowers"},{"effect":"Subject to strict reporting of foreign contacts, foreign money bans for ballot initiatives, expanded disclaimer requirements for paid online communications, and online ad archive mandates.","group":"Political Committees and Campaigns"},{"effect":"Required to sign ethics pledges restricting post-government lobbying, face stricter Hatch Act enforcement and penalties, and are barred from certain corporate roles if convicted of specific white-collar crimes.","group":"Executive Branch Appointees"}],"key_provisions":["Prevents presidential self-pardons, requires submission of certain pardon-related prosecution materials to Congress, and updates bribery laws to include candidates for President and Vice President.","Tolls statutes of limitations for federal criminal offenses committed by a sitting President or Vice President and revokes certain Former Presidents Act benefits upon felony conviction.","Prohibits senior federal officials from accepting foreign payments or emoluments without the consent of Congress, creating reporting mechanisms, civil actions, and penalties.","Expands enforcement mechanisms for congressional subpoenas, including expedited court procedures, document logs, and potential monetary penalties for agency heads.","Strengthens the Congressional Budget and Impoundment Control Act of 1974 by imposing stricter timelines, agency reporting requirements, and Comptroller General litigation authorities.","Reformulates the National Emergencies Act to require joint resolutions of approval from Congress for national emergency declarations and specified emergency powers to remain active.","Establishes strict campaign finance rules regarding foreign contacts, including mandatory reporting of contacts involving foreign nationals, opposition research, and online political advertisements."],"missing_information":["Exact fiscal impact estimates or budgetary costs associated with establishing new offices, reporting mandates, and three-judge court proceedings are not provided in the text."],"plain_summary":"H.R. 8831, titled the \"Protecting Our Democracy Act,\" proposes a wide array of government reforms. The bill aims to prevent abuses of executive and presidential power, strengthen congressional checks and balances, increase transparency across federal agencies, establish stricter ethics and emoluments enforcement, protect whistleblowers, and defend elections against foreign interference.","significance":"Sweeping"},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-11-04T22:49:14+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr8831/BILLS-119hr8831ih.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Protecting Our Democracy Act","viability":31.8,"viabil